      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The high probability of soil liquefaction during moderate seismic events presents a very serious, high-consequence risk for a large structure. This is not a minor issue, but it is not necessarily an absolute dealbreaker if significant mitigation is planned. The project would likely require deep foundation systems, such as driven piles or ground improvement techniques, to stabilize the loose, saturated sands against liquefaction. You should argue that these necessary, substantial engineering costs must be fully integrated into the budget and planning to justify the gamble.",
      "source": "target",
